WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.302
"Can a Plant-Based Diet Reverse Type 2 Diabetes?"

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.600
Diabetes is a leading
cause of death worldwide

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.040
with an estimated
1.5 million deaths each year

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.360
directly attributable
to diabetes,

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.160
primarily type 2 diabetes.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.360
And the disease is a major cause
of other health complications;

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.960
kidney failure, heart attacks,

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.920
strokes,
and lower limb amputations.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.120
Along with those conditions
goes rising healthcare costs.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.120
For example,
in the United States,

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.160
diabetes makes the list for
the top five medical conditions

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.760
accounting for a third
of all medical expenditures.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.120
And spending more than doubled
over 20 years.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.640
Diabetes is the only disease

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.520
for which cost per person
has increased significantly

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:48.240
for these top five
medical conditions,

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:52.240
coming in close
to $3,400 per person.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.240
The majority of those costs
come from prescription medications.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.200
And, while diabetes medications
can be a very important tool

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.600
for controlling
blood glucose levels,

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.240
what if there were another way?

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:06.960
Could a plant-based diet
be the solution,

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:12.480
not only to diabetes prevention
but to type 2 diabetes treatment?

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.080
And not just any treatment,

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:18.080
but actually with the goal
of diabetes remission.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.760
The American College
of Lifestyle Medicine

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:22.960
convened a group of experts including
representatives from major groups

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.280
like the American
College of Cardiology,

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:27.440
the American Heart Association,

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.520
the Academy
of Nutrition and Dietetics,

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:30.880
the list goes on,

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:33.840
who reviewed the available
evidence on dietary interventions

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.200
for type 2 diabetes
treatment for remission,

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.880
and reached agreement
on three key issues.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:45.520
First, type 2 diabetes remission
should be defined as having HbA1c,

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.600
a marker of blood
glucose control,

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.240
below 6.5 percent for
at least three months

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:53.840
with no surgery, devices,
or active drug therapy

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:55.920
being used to
lower blood sugars.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.320
Second, diet, as a primary
intervention for type 2 diabetes

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.200
can achieve remission in many adults

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.320
and is related to the intensity
of the intervention.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.960
And, finally, the big one,

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:10.560
diet as a primary intervention

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.520
is the most effective
in achieving remission

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:16.160
when emphasizing whole,
plant-based foods,

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:20.720
with minimal consumption
of animal products.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.880
Why is this so profound?

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:26.400
In addition to experts from all
these different groups agreeing,

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.320
nutrition therapy
is not usually discussed

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:31.520
in the context of remission,
but rather as an add-on

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:34.480
to go with whatever drugs are
prescribed for blood sugar control,

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:38.240
or as a way to help delay
or prevent complications.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:40.880
In this consensus statement,
remission was endorsed

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:43.920
as the clinical goal
for type 2 diabetes,

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.600
and it is most
optimally attained

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.760
using a whole-food,
plant-based diet

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.640
that emphasizes
unrefined plant foods

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.880
and eliminates
or minimizes animal foods

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:55.360
and refined foods,
and, of course,

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.960
includes moderate exercise

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:01.040
that we all should be
getting on a regular basis.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:02.720
Oh, and critically,

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:06.000
the intervention meant to
help with type 2 diabetes

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.360
shouldn't cause adverse
health effects itself,

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.920
such as very low-carb
ketogenic diets,

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.640
which might appear to help
with blood glucose control,

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:19.120
but in fact produce negative
cardiometabolic side effects.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:21.760
Here's what can happen after
treatment with a high-fiber,

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.080
low-fat, plant-predominant diet.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.640
The authors wanted to show
the feasibility

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.680
of medication reduction
and type 2 diabetes remission

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.920
using a lifestyle-based
intervention

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.800
without drastically
cutting calories.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:37.760
Patients with diabetes
were referred to a wellness clinic

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:41.120
and received information on
adopting a plant-predominant diet

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:44.400
along with addressing
other major risk factors.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.960
Importantly, these patients
didn't self-select

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:50.080
into a specific lifestyle
medicine treatment program.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.880
They were simply presented
with lifestyle prescriptions

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.120
as part of their routine
medical care.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:56.800
What a wild idea!

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:58.880
Here's a visual
of the plant-predominant diet

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:02.800
they were encouraged to follow—
about 95 percent plants

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:07.360
with a lot of veggies, beans,
whole grains, fruits, and seeds.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:09.680
The researchers took
a closer look at those patients

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:12.480
who had adopted the recommended
plant-centric diet

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.560
and successfully decreased
their blood sugar

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:16.720
to non-diabetic ranges.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:19.040
How many people
experienced remission?

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:20.560
More than a third of them

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:24.720
and almost half with HbA1c
levels below 6.5 percent

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:27.360
were able to discontinue
all medications—

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:30.320
they just hadn't yet reached
the three consecutive months

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:32.000
of testing required
to get the label

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.720
for "official remission."

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:38.240
A lifestyle-based intervention,
primarily focused on education

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:40.480
about the benefits
of a plant-predominant diet

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:43.440
for diabetes treatment
and remission,

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:46.080
resulted in decreased
blood glucose markers

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:48.960
to levels achieving
both reduction of medications

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:52.160
and remission
of type 2 diabetes,

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:55.440
highlighting the promising potential
for a plant-predominant diet

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.640
to confer immediate
and long-term benefit

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:03.009
including reducing complications
of type 2 diabetes.

